  "term": "ventromedial nucleus",
  "definition": "The ventromedial nucleus is a region of the hypothalamus. In this source, it is described as one of the brain areas examined for stress-related corticotropin-releasing factor receptor gene expression, including sex-dependent effects after early life pain and later fear conditioning.",
